Syntax definitions linked onto syntect 5.3's default newlines set by build.rs.
syntect 5.3 does not implement Sublime's `extends` key, so the current
sublimehq TypeScript package cannot be vendored as-is. TypeScript.sublime-syntax
embeds the bundled JavaScript grammar (scope:source.js). A keyword overlay was
not added: syntect applies `with_prototype` inside strings and comments.
JSONC.sublime-syntax is a small JSON-with-comments grammar written for this
editor. Neither file is an upstream copy.

